-- title:
--   Involution of the level-4q function field scaling level-4 q-expansions
-- statement:
--   Work inside the field $\mathbb{Q}(\!(\mathfrak q)\!)$ of rational Laurent series. For $N \neq 0$ let $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,N$ denote the ring endomorphism of Laurent series that multiplies all exponents by $N$ (the `embDomain` homomorphism along $g \mapsto Ng$), and let `modularFunctionFieldFull N` be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(\mathfrak q)\!)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set of series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,(jq)$ for the nonzero divisors $d \mid N$, i.e. by the degeneracies $j(\mathfrak q^{d})$ of the $j$-expansion. The assertion is: for every prime $q$ with $q \neq 2$ there exists a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of `modularFunctionFieldFull (4 * q)` such that (i) for every element $x$ of that field whose underlying Laurent series lies in the subfield `modularFunctionFieldFull 4` (generated by $j(\mathfrak q),\,j(\mathfrak q^{2}),\,j(\mathfrak q^{4})$), the Laurent series underlying $\sigma(x)$ equals $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,q$ applied to that of $x$, that is $\sigma(x) = x(\mathfrak q^{q})$; and (ii) $\sigma(\sigma(x)) = x$ for all $x$. Only the behaviour of $\sigma$ on the level-$4$ subfield is recorded, not the full swap of all generators.
--
--   This is the partial Atkin–Lehner involution $W_q$ of $X_0(4q)$, read on $q$-expansions and packaged in a data-free form: an involutive $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism of the level-$4q$ $q$-expansion field which on the level-$4$ subfield is the substitution $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{q}$. It is used in the analysis of the minimal polynomial of $\lambda(\mathfrak q^{q})$ over the level-$4$ field, in [`ModularCurve.intCoeffs_minpoly_lambdaNModC_coeff`](thm.html#ModularCurve.intCoeffs_minpoly_lambdaNModC_coeff) and [`ModularCurve.minpoly_lambdaNModC_coeff_coeff_eq_zero_of_neg`](thm.html#ModularCurve.minpoly_lambdaNModC_coeff_coeff_eq_zero_of_neg).
